# Cloudflare Pages static asset headers.
# BUG FIX (user report) — the landing-page MP4s live at a fixed filename
# (/media/crewboss-saas-16x9.mp4, /media/crewboss-saas-9x16.mp4) that doesn't
# change between deploys, unlike the JS/CSS bundle (which Vite content-
# hashes into its filename, so a new build is automatically a new URL).
# Without an explicit Cache-Control, both the browser and Cloudflare's
# edge cache were very likely still serving the OLD video bytes after a
# redeploy — the user kept seeing an old render (with the on-page player
# chrome baked into the pixels) even after the source pipeline was
# fixed and the file was overwritten. LandingPage.tsx now also appends
# a version query string, but this header is the real defense: cap how
# long any cache is allowed to serve a copy before checking again.
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
